(ned -- helper for cal_a_zero. ONE SUB PER FILE: LinuxCNC resolves)
(subroutines through SUBROUTINE_PATH, and a second sub defined in)
(the calling file is NOT found -- "EOF in file ... seeking o-word",)
(reproduced offline with rs274. Shared setup arrives in GLOBAL)
(parameters; the result goes back the same way.)

(======================== helper: ONE wall touch ===========================)
(  #1 = plunge depth below the puck top)
(  #2 = approach: 1 = come from hover and go out to the standoff first,)
(                 0 = ALREADY at the backoff standoff, just change depth)
(  #3 = retract:  1 = finish back at hover, 0 = stay at the backoff standoff)
(Returns the touch Y in #<_ca_ty>.)

(Operator 2026-08-03: travelling between the two plunge depths at the backoff)
(standoff is safe enough -- no climbing back over the puck between touches.)
(That Z move is still a G38.3, so a surprise contact stops the machine rather)
(than driving through it.)

o<ca_touch> sub
  #<dep>      = #1
  #<approach> = #2
  #<retract>  = #3

  o100 if [#<approach> NE 0]
    (hover, then out to the standoff OUTSIDE the puck)
    G90
    G1 Z[#<_ca_top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
    G1 X#<_ca_cx> Y[#<_ca_cy> + #<_ca_side> * #<_ca_stand>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]

    (protective descent: if this TRIPS, the standoff is still over the puck --)
    (the puck is wider than the standoff. Never plunge blind.)
    G91
    G38.3 Z-[#<_ca_safe> + #<dep>] F[#<_ca_fck>]
    o105 if [#5070 EQ 1]
      G90
      G1 Z[#<_ca_top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
      M65 P3
      M50 P1
      (abort, CAL A: contact while descending at the standoff - the puck is wider than the standoff. Increase _ca_stand.)
    o105 endif
  o100 else
    (already alongside the puck: change depth right here, protected)
    G90
    G38.3 Z[#<_ca_top> - #<dep>] F[#<_ca_fck>]
    o106 if [#5070 EQ 1]
      G90
      G1 Z[#<_ca_top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
      M65 P3
      M50 P1
      (abort, CAL A: contact while changing depth at the backoff standoff - something is beside the puck that should not be.)
    o106 endif
    G91
  o100 endif

  (probe INWARD toward the axis; the wall stops us)
  G38.3 Y[0 - #<_ca_side> * #<_ca_reach>] F[#<_ca_fpr>]
  o110 if [#5070 EQ 0]
    G90
    G1 Z[#<_ca_top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
    M65 P3
    M50 P1
    (abort, CAL A: no contact driving inward. The ROD must protrude far enough that its shaft still spans the puck at this depth - a 65 mm plunge needs more than 65 mm of rod below the holder. Check the stickout, the standoff and the reach.)
  o110 endif
  G1 Y[#<_ca_side> * #<_ca_back>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
  G38.2 Y[0 - #<_ca_side> * [#<_ca_back> + 1]] F[#<_ca_fla>]
  #<_ca_ty> = #5062

  (RELEASE PROVEN, NOT GUESSED. G38.5 backs off until the probe OPENS and)
  (stops there -- "probe until no contact away from work, no error", the form)
  (used by stock rectangle_probe.ngc. A blind G1 of a guessed distance can)
  (leave the rod still touching, and then the FIRST non-probe move of the)
  (NEXT cycle dies with "probe tripped during non-probe move" -- one abort)
  (poisoning every run after it, which is what happened 2026-08-03. This is)
  (not a contact-quality question: it is about never issuing an ordinary move)
  (while the probe is made.)
  (this standoff is what the next touch reuses)
  G38.5 Y[#<_ca_side> * 2 * #<_ca_back>] F[#<_ca_fla>]
  G1 Y[#<_ca_side> * #<_ca_back>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
  G90

  o120 if [#<retract> NE 0]
    G1 Z[#<_ca_top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
  o120 endif
o<ca_touch> endsub

M2 (end helper)
